<h1>Patrick Kevin Coughlin</h1>
<p>Judge up for retention, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Incumbent.</p>
<p>Circuit Court of Cook County</p>
<h2>Ratings</h2>
<ul>
<li>Chicago Bar Association: <a href="https://www.chicagobar.org/votejudges#:~:text=Patrick%20Kevin%20Coughlin" rel="nofollow noopener">Qualified</a></li>
<li>Illinois State Bar Association: <a href="https://www.isba.org/judicial-elections/counties/cook#:~:text=Patrick%20Kevin%20Coughlin" rel="nofollow noopener">Yes</a></li>
<li>Injustice Watch: <a href="https://2026retention.injusticewatch.org/candidate/patrick-kevin-coughlin-35905" rel="nofollow noopener">Former prosecutor</a></li>
</ul>
<h2>Record</h2>
<p>Elected to the Circuit Court in 2014; hears felony cases at the Markham courthouse, where he has spent most of his judicial career. Injustice Watch reports that the appellate court overturned his 38-year sentence for Lavert Bonner, who was 17 when he shot and killed Lawrence Mack in 2010, with the majority writing that the length was not justified given Coughlin&#39;s own finding that Bonner could be rehabilitated; one judge dissented. He said court rules bar him from commenting on a pending case. A judge stays on the bench with a yes from 60 percent of voters.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Cook County assistant state&#39;s attorney, finishing as deputy bureau chief in the narcotics division (1996-2014). Law degree from DePaul University (1996).</p>
